   "worked_solution": [
      {
         "step": 1,
         "text": "\\( \\frac{dx}{dt} = \\frac{2 t}{t^{2} + 1} + 3 \\) and, by the chain rule, \\( \\frac{dy}{dt} = - 3 t e^{- \\frac{t^{2}}{4}} \\).",
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99049",
         "rule_named": "component derivatives"
      },
      {
         "step": 2,
         "text": "At \\( t = \\frac{3}{2} \\), \\( \\frac{dx}{dt} = \\frac{51}{13} \\) and \\( \\frac{dy}{dt} \\approx -2.564 \\) (more places kept).",
         "mathjson": -2.5640227112891534,
         "point_type_id": "BC-PT-99005",
         "rule_named": "evaluate at the time"
      },
      {
         "step": 3,
         "text": "The slope is \\( \\frac{dy/dt}{dx/dt} = \\frac{y'(\\frac{3}{2})}{x'(\\frac{3}{2})} \\approx -0.654 \\).",
